    "updated_at": "2018-08-02T16:33:47Z",
    "body": "Hmm, no response from the CCed people. Trying again, and throwing in @smaug---- for good measure: do Chrome/Safari/Firefox have any interest in aligning with the current spec and allowing multiple space-separated values for accesskey, falling back to later ones if the first ones don't work?\r\n\r\nIf not (or if we continue to get no response), we should definitely update the spec to reflect reality; thanks @chaals for the catch. We'd need to be more precise in how we do this; in particular we'd need a rigorous definition for what is accepted, since \"produced with a single key\" or the fork's phrasing of \"may strip content\" are not interoperably implementable. It sounds like there's another issue here around multiple code points, which we may want to tackle at the same time or separately.\r\n\r\nFor both issues, we'll need extensive web platform tests (using webdriver for the key triggering) as part of the process for landing specification changes. That would probably be a good place to start, as it also gives us more insight into what browsers currently do. @chaals, are you interested in working on that?",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
