    "body": "I checked in with @melanierichards to get her view on this:\r\n\r\n>I’m not aware of any strong precedent that would make us go one way or another. The attitude in accessibility w/r/t accesskey seems to be: “here be dragons”. Problems cited are around potential conflicts with the browser and especially with screen readers, inconsistencies between browsers, lack of standardization of individual accesskey values, internationalization concerns, etc.\r\n>\r\n>Because the guidance is to be very careful with access keys and maybe not use them, […] we could keep our behavior, or move to another one. Devs will have to check their code and make sure they got their intended behavior. 😊 MDN, which gets more air time with the general dev population than the specs, mentions the ability for space-separated keys but acknowledges the IE/Edge behavior.\r\n\r\nSo I think we're game, if the consensus is to move to space-separated tokens or some other more clearly defined behavior.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
