    "body": "@domenic wrote\r\n\r\n>we'll need extensive web platform tests (using webdriver for the key triggering) as part of the process for landing specification changes. That would probably be a good place to start, as it also gives us more insight into what browsers currently do.\r\n\r\nI don't have the time to repeat this work now, but if you look at the changes in the W3C HTML specification you can find the various manual tests that were made and run in browsers over the last few years. It appears that nothing has changed over that time frame, although copying those to WPT tests will presumably simplify life for browser developers in the future.\r\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
